\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves edge down as U.S. yields rise\b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2008\par 01:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details)\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, May 9 (Reuters) - Japan's foreign reserves stood at $1.004 trillion at the end of April, down slightly from a record high hit a month earlier, partly because higher U.S. yields cut the value of U.S. bonds held in the stockpile.\par \par \uc2 It was the first monthly fall in nearly a year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) said on Friday. [JPRES=ECI]\par \par \uc2 At the end of March, Japan's reserves, the world's second largest after China, had been a record high of $1.016 trillion.\par \par \uc2 The yield on the benchmark 10-year U.S. Treasury note <US10TY=RR> rose to 3.732 percent at the end of April from 3.413 percent at the end of March, according to finance ministry data.\par \par \uc2 A MOF official told reporters that the euro's fall against the dollar reduced the value of euro-denominated bonds in the reserves. Lower gold prices also pushed down the reserves in doller terms, he added.\par \par \uc2 The ministry said the euro <EUR=> fell to $1.5622 at the end of April from $1.5788 at the end of March, while prices of gold <XAU=> fell to $871.0 an ounce from $993.5 an ounce.\par \par \uc2 The ministry does not disclose the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  breakdown of Japan's international reserves, but most is in U.S. dollars as past \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken the form of dollar buying.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves ballooned after yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  worth a record 20 trillion yen ($193 billion) in 2003 and a further 15 trillion yen in the first three months of 2004, as the government waged a campaign to prevent a rapid rise in the yen from derailing Japan's then-fragile economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo has stayed out of the market since then. JAPAN OFFICIAL RESERVE ASSETS (in billion dollars)\par \par \uc2 END-APRIL END-MAR YEAR-AGO TOTAL 1,003.836 1,015.587 915.623 To view the full tables, go to the website of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mof.go.jp/english/e1c006.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.mof.go.jp/english/e1c006.htm}}}\uc2  ($1=103.75 Yen) (Reporting by Yoko Nishikawa; Editing by Hugh Lawson)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/RESERVES (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|NAT|U|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080508e458002j6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
