\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Japan, Euro zone ministers seek G7 message on  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Leika Kihara   \par \uc2 880 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2008\par 02:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds Trichet on cross-border \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  liquidity, updates prices)   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, April 4 (Reuters) - Japanese and Euro zone finance ministers called for G7 finance leaders meeting next week to seek a curb on excessive exchange-rate movements, amid growing concern over the economic effects of a sliding dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "It is important for the G7 members to confirm their shared understanding that excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate moves are undesirable for economic growth," Japanese Finance Minister Fukushiro Nukaga told reporters on Friday, when asked whether the dollar's broad downtrend would be discussed at the G7 meeting.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar tumbled to an all-time low of $1.5904 per euro <EUR=> and to a 13-year low below 96 yen <JPY=> last month on fears the U.S. economy, battered by an ailing housing market and a deeply wounded banking sector, would enter a recession.   \par \par \uc2 It has bounced back somewhat since, though was struggling against both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday in volatile trade after a worse than expected U.S. jobs report.   \par \par \uc2 The euro <EUR=> was up 0.3 percent at $1.5733 in late New York trade while the dollar traded 0.5 percent lower against the yen at 101.86 yen <JPY=>. It fell 0.3 percent against a basket of six \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 71.988 <.DXY>.   \par \par \uc2 The greenback has fallen around 6 percent on a trade-weighted basis in the past month -- raising fears in Europe and Japan that businesses will lose out to cheaper rivals trading in U.S. dollars.   \par \par \uc2 "Our concern is well-known, we don't like excessive volatility and disorderly rate moves, they are harming worldwide economic growth and we will stick to that line," Eurogroup chief Jean-Claude Juncker told reporters late on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Ministers from the 15 countries using the euro and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or the Eurogroup, are meeting in the Slovenian town of Brdo, close to Ljubljana, to discuss the economy at a regular meeting and agree on their call to Group of Seven rich economies, which meet next Friday in Washington. [ID:nL04397323]   \par \par \uc2 MORE COMMUNICATION NEEDED   \par \par \uc2 Nukaga said the G7 finance ministers and central bankers needed to communicate closely to stabilise financial markets at a time global economic growth appears to be slowing.   \par \par \uc2 The G7 has said in past meeting communiques that excess volatility and disorderly movements in exchange rates were undesirable.   \par \par \uc2 Markets watch communique wording on exchange rates closely, because all G7 members agree on the phrasing, so it could give the first signal of a deal on concerted action in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.   \par \par \uc2 European countries have been vocal in expressing concern over the euro's sharp rises against the dollar as such moves would hurt the competitive advantage of the region's exports. French Economy Minister Christine Lagarde said on Thursday that the current situation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was "painful" for euro zone economies.   \par \par \uc2 Japan's growth also relies heavily on exporters, with  \uc2 Sony Corp\uc2  , the maker of PlayStation game machines, saying on Thursday that each one yen rise against the U.S. dollar cost the company about $59 million. [ID:nTP96194]   \par \par \uc2 But big Japanese manufacturers have not complained much about the stronger yen and monetary authorities in Tokyo have largely taken a hands-off approach, partly because the nation's exports have continued to rise despite slowing U.S. growth.   \par \par \uc2 Nukaga toned up his warning against rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves when the yen spiked last month, saying that he felt the moves were excessive and that the ministry was watching with great interest.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  STILL A RISK   \par \par \uc2 With the yen having stabilised, few market players expect Tokyo to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but some warn against complacency.   \par \par \uc2 "I don't think \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  now but if the dollar falls below 90 yen, it would be a different story," said Satoru Ogasawara, an economist at  \uc2 Credit Suisse.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers are surely worried about the dollar falling too much. It's too early to rule out the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  just yet," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  massively in 2003 and early 2004 to prevent a rapid rise in the yen from aggravating deflation and derailing a fragile export-led recovery. But it has not stepped in since.   \par \par \uc2 The world's central banks are also considering new measures to ease the pain in money markets, Japan's Jiji news wire reported on Friday, without citing sources.   \par \par \uc2 The central banks of Japan, Europe, the United States and some developing countries were considering a system to allow a private bank in one country to borrow funds from another country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it had collateral set aside at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its own country, Jiji said.   \par \par \uc2 Asked in Brdo to confirm the report, ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet said no decision had been taken as yet.   \par \par \uc2 "I will only say that there are... reflections at the level of constituency of central banks on improving the situation. But I cannot say anything else on that particular point. If and when we have something to make public we will make it public."   \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Krista Hughes in Brdo, Slovenia)   \par \par \uc2 G7/ (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|J|NAT|UKI|ABX|BNX|FUN|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080404e4440001b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
