\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  did not  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market in March   \b0\par\par\uc2 218 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 12:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 31 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not conduct any \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between Feb. 28 and March 27 despite the dollar's slide to 13-year lows below 96 yen, \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Japan has stayed out of the market for four years, the longest stretch in MOF data going back to 1991.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to 95.77 yen <JPY=> earlier in March, the lowest since August 1995, after ailing U.S. investment bank  \uc2 Bear Stearns\uc2  agreed to be taken over by  \uc2 JPMorgan Chase.\par \par \uc2 The news was seen as underscoring how damaging the credit market turmoil had been for Wall Street and triggered a dollar sell-off.   \par \par \uc2 The last time Japanese authorities sold yen to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise was on March 16, 2004, when it was trading at about 108.60 to the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Japan sold 35 trillion yen ($350 billion) in the 15 months to March 2004 to weaken the yen due to concerns that excessive yen strength could weaken overseas demand for Japanese exports and hurt the economy. ($1=100.00 Yen) (Reporting by Masayuki Kitano)   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|NAT|J|SI|RBN|UKI|AUF|ND|ABN|M|E|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|U   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080331e43v000v1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
