\par\par \b \uc2 BOJ may cut rates despite leadership turmoil-Goldman\b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 06:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 19 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan is likely to cut interest rates by the end of April due to growing downside risks for the economy, a sharp tightening in financial conditions and expectations of more Federal Reserve rate cuts, Goldman Sachs said in a report on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2  A political standoff over who will head the BOJ after Governor Toshihiko Fukui steps down on Wednesday is unlikely to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from cutting rates 25 basis points to 0.25 percent, said Goldman's chief Japan economist Tetsufumi Yamakawa.\par \par \uc2  "The turbulence surrounding the BOJ leadership changeover need not impede policy change," Yamakawa said in the report.\par \par \uc2  Japanese interest rates at 0.5 percent are already near rock bottom, but Goldman said it looked as if the country had been in recession since the last quarter of last year, with U.S. weakness and abrupt rises in the yen added spurs for a rate cut.\par \par \uc2  Most market players currently expect the BOJ to keep interest rates on hold for the rest of this year.\par \par \uc2  Although the yen has surged as much as 30 percent against the dollar since the middle of last year, Yamakawa said authorities in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a major exporter, were unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold back the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.\par \par \uc2  A stronger yen makes Japanese goods less competitive in overseas markets and cuts into profits earned abroad when repatriated to Japan.\par \par \uc2  But Yamakawa said the yen was still low by the measure of effective exchange rates, while \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would draw criticism from China and elsewhere in Asia. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market would be more costly following \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2003 and early 2004, he added. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/GOLDMAN|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080319e43j00070\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
