\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar above 13-year lows vs yen but seen fragile   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Masayuki Kitano   \par \uc2 826 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 04:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 18 (Reuters) - The dollar held above its lowest level against the yen in nearly 13 years and a record low versus the euro on Tuesday, but was seen susceptible to more declines on worries about the U.S. financial system.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar plunged on Monday after the Federal Reserve took the emergency step of cutting its discount rate on Sunday and opened up discount window lending to major investment banks, a tool not used since the Great Depression.   \par \par \uc2 The steps, which accompanied  \uc2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\uc2 's decision to buy stricken rival  \uc2 Bear Stearns\uc2  at a rock-bottom price of $2 a share, was seen as highlighting the depths of the damage caused by the tumult in credit markets and sparked a dollar sell-off.   \par \par \uc2 "The market is still nervous about the U.S. financial system and is now talking about which financial firms are looking dangerous and which are not," said Shuichi Kanehira, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at  \uc2 Mizuho Corporate Bank.\par \par \uc2 "Given this uncertainty, the dollar will stay weak," he said.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell 0.2 percent from late U.S. trading on Monday to around 97.20 yen It fell as low as 95.77 yen on Monday on electronic trading platform EBS, the lowest in more than 12-\u189\'00\'BD years.   \par \par \uc2 The yen showed a subdued reaction to news that the Japanese government had nominated a former top finance ministry official, Koji Tanami, as its second candidate to run the Bank of Japan after Toshihiko Fukui retires on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 "The market is more focused on the U.S. credit crunch, and I do not get the sense that traders will regard this as a factor," said a trader for a Japanese trust bank.   \par \par \uc2 The name surprised market players and it was hard to say what kind of stance Tanami has on monetary policy and whether his nomination would be approved by opposition parties, they said.   \par \par \uc2 The opposition have the power to veto the appointment through their control of parliament's upper house.   \par \par \uc2 The euro edged up 0.3 percent from late New York to around $1.5770 but was below a record $1.5905 struck on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 FED'S RATE DECISION   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the market was in a wait-and-see mode ahead of a Fed policy meeting and quarterly earnings announcements by U.S. investment banks  \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  and  \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  later on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 The Federal Reserve is widely expected to cut interest rates by 1 percentage point to 2 percent at a policy meeting on Tuesday, and investors see a small chance of an even deeper cut.   \par \par \uc2 U.S. short-term interest rate futures show that investors see a roughly 10 percent chance of the Fed cutting interest rates by 1.25 percentage point on Tuesday. The chances of a 1 percentage point cut are seen at roughly 90 percent.   \par \par \uc2 "The dollar could come under pressure if the size of the Fed rate cut turns out to be 75 basis points and that leads to a fall in U.S. share prices," said the trader for a Japanese trust bank.   \par \par \uc2 Investors are also watching to see if the Fed will come out with any extra steps in addition to lowering interest rates, the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar's sharp sell-off on Monday has caused traders to fret about the possibility of joint dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by U.S., Japanese and European authorities.   \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials again weighed in on Tuesday on movements in financial markets and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The nation's top financial diplomat, Naoyuki Shinohara, said he was told by Prime Minister Yasuo Fukuda to keep in close contact with other Group of Seven members on developments in global financial markets.   \par \par \uc2 In addition, Finance Minister Fukushiro Nukaga said the government would monitor \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in cooperation with the U.S. and European authorities, adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves have been excessively volatile. His remarks were similar to what he said on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Despite such rhetoric, some market players said the chances of joint action to prop up the dollar seemed low at this point.   \par \par \uc2 Masafumi Yamamoto, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the  \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2 , said even coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might not be very effective unless U.S. authorities first took steps such as injecting public funds into the financial system.   \par \par \uc2 Although officials at the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have recently expressed concern about "excessive" moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market players say the ECB may be willing to accept the euro's surge against the dollar to help rein in inflation.   \par \par \uc2 ECB executive board member Juergen Stark said on Tuesday that commodity prices and second round inflation effects are among the biggest risks to price stability, according to an interview with a business daily in Portugal.   \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Satomi Noguchi, Editing by Michael Watson)   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 2, GRAPHIC)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080318e43i0004q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
