\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Dollar's nosedive stirs joint  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  jitters   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Satomi Noguchi   \par \uc2 563 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 05:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, comments)   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 17 (Reuters) - The dollar's sharp slide to 13-year lows against the yen and fresh all-time lows versus the euro on Monday is stoking jitters about the possibility of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "The speed of the slide in the dollar/yen is so rapid that U.S. action alone can no longer stop the dollar's downward trend," said Koichi Ogawa, chief portfolio manager at Daiwa SB Investment.   \par \par \uc2 "The time is ripe for coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by U.S., European and Japanese authorities."   \par \par \uc2 Remarks on Monday by Japanese Finance Minister Fukushiro Nukaga also kept investors on their toes.   \par \par \uc2 "We will cooperate with European and U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities and will monitor markets very carefully," Nukaga told reporters, adding that the latest moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets had been excessively volatile and that he would watch markets carefully.   \par \par \uc2 Nukaga's comments gave a slight lift to the dollar, which last traded near 97 yen after earlier dropping by over 3 percent to a 13-year low of 95.77 yen on electronic trading platform EBS.   \par \par \uc2 "His comments were different from usual so that led to some speculation about joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Hiroshi Yoshida, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at  \uc2 Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Yoshida said, however, that while some traders thought coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a possibility, there weren't many who believed that the chances of such action were high.   \par \par \uc2 The euro stood at $1.5843 after having trimmed some gains since earlier jumping 1.5 percent to $1.5905 the highest since the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was launched in 1999.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar plummetted against the yen and euro on investor fears that more financial institutions could become casualties in the widening U.S. financial crisis that led to  \uc2 JPMorgan Chase\uc2  acquiring investment bank  \uc2 Bear Stearns\par \par \uc2 Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Yoshida said that the impact of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely increase if authorities were to buy dollars against both the yen and the euro.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was in a near state of panic, and some said coordinated dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may conceivably happen as soon as markets in London open on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 "Solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems difficult, but given this market turmoil, the US and Europe could move and conduct coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said a senior options trader at a Japanese bank in Tokyo.   \par \par \uc2 There was still some scepticism, however, about the likelihood for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "The Fed's dollar position has been relaxed so far, and will most probably remain so," Benedikt Germanier, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 UBS\uc2  said in a research note.   \par \par \uc2 "Joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems also less likely as the ECB is busy managing inflation expectations," he said, adding that the last joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had taken place in September 2000 to stem a decline in the euro.   \par \par \uc2 In addition, Japanese authorities had "failed to draw a line in the sand", he said.   \par \par \uc2 "The risk of an indifferent position will be a disorderly fall in the dollar accompanied by a further decline in U.S. equities and sharply rising yields. This would have very negative consequences on the real economy as well," Germanier added.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|SXNA   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080317e43h000ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
