\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -US dollar slumps in wake of Fed's emergency measures   \b0\par\par\uc2 697 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 22:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds comment)   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar tumbled to a 12-1/2 year low against the Japanese yen Monday, and also saw record lows against the euro and the Swiss franc, as emergency liquidity-boosting measures by the Federal Reserve over the weekend failed to ease worries about the U.S. financial system.   \par \par \uc2 The greenback sold off in reaction to the Fed cutting its discount rate by 25 basis points to 3.25 percent on Sunday and after the opening up of the Fed's discount window lending to major investment banks, a tool not used since the Great Depression.   \par \par \uc2 The Fed's move accompanied the purchase of  \uc2 Bear Stearns\uc2  by  \uc2 JPMorgan Chase\uc2  for just $2 a share, less than one-tenth of the bank's share price on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar slid as much as 3.0 percent to below 96.00 yen, its lowest since 1995, bringing year-to-date losses to more than 13 percent.   \par \par \uc2 "The Fed's announcement to triple the maximum maturity of discount window loans to 90 days and its $30 billion in funding of  \uc2 Bear Stearns\uc2  less liquid assets not only indicated the grave situation posed to the counter party risk involved, but also highlights the increased ineffectiveness of the Fed's historic liquidity injections yet to date," said Ashraf Laidi, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist, CMC Markets U.S. in a research note to clients.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell as low as 95.77 yen according to Reuters data, and saw historic lows 0.9637 Swiss francs after breaking below parity last week.   \par \par \uc2 The euro rose as high as $1.5904, having already added around 4.0 percent in the first two weeks of March, roughly doubling its year-to-date gains. It last traded at $1.5745.   \par \par \uc2 Matthew Strauss, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at RBC Capital in Toronto, said that despite the high levels in dollar-yen and rumors of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there were no clear indications the Japanese government is ready to take action to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating further.   \par \par \uc2 Implied volatility, a key component of option pricing, in dollar/yen surged to its highest levels in around a decade both on the one-week and one-month horizon.   \par \par \uc2 In another report on Monday, the U.S. Treasury Department said net overall capital flows in the country fell to its lowest level in four months in January. The inflows were not sufficient to cover the month's U.S. trade deficit.   \par \par \uc2 "Today's TICs report takes a back seat to tomorrow's FOMC's decision, with market expectations regarding the size of the anticipated cut all over the map," Michael Woolfolk, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 The Bank of New York\uc2  Mellon, said in a note.   \par \par \uc2 Short-term U.S. Treasury yields fell to five-year lows as investors expect the Fed could cut overnight rates by up to a full percentage point at its policy meeting on Tuesday.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?   \par \par \uc2 The rapid U.S. dollar fall fanned talk of possible coordinated dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from major central banks other than the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "From the ECB point of view, these are moves which are not easy to ignore," Dresdner Kleinwort \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Michael Klawitter said in Frankfurt.   \par \par \uc2 The euro saw some volatility when Market News International, citing a source, said the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Governing Council will likely express concern about the euro's rapid surge against the dollar in a coordinated "verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " over the next several days and weeks.   \par \par \uc2 But the sources noted that "verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " doesn't mean actual \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the euro's rise against a weak dollar and the euro's moves were shortlived.   \par \par \uc2 Central banks in Europe, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. last jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September 2000, propping up the euro after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit an all-time low below $0.85, a loss of nearly 30 percent of its value from its January 1999 launch.   \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Nick Olivari and Vivianne Rodrigues)   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 9)|LANGEN|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080316e43g000pe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
