\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day   \b0\par\par\uc2 610 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 03:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: RISING YEN WORRIES JAPAN BUT NO HINTS OF ACTION YET    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's top economy officials voiced renewed concerns Friday about the dollar's recent rapid fall against the yen, but they provided few hints on whether \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to help the embattled U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0142 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBA GOV SAYS CPI INFLATION PEAK LIKELY TO BE AROUND 4%    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor, Glenn Stevens, said the peak in consumer price index inflation in Australia will likely be around 4%, a good result when compared with inflation spikes in the past and given the major global economic change currently underway. (published 2346 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NZ 4Q MANUFACTURING SALES JUMP 8.3%; DAIRY, MEAT RISE    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's manufacturing sales rose sharply in the fourth quarter of 2007, pushed up by a strong rise in meat and dairy product manufacturing, official data published Friday showed. (published 2334 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MALAYSIA 3-PARTY OPPOSITION SIGNS AGREEMENT TO END SQUABBLING    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Officials say Malaysia's three-party opposition alliance has signed a written agreement to end public squabbling over the leadership of a state government. (published 0136 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ(3/14) UPDATE: LAWMAKERS ALIGN ON PLAN TO INSURE MORTGAGES    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WASHINGTON -- Congressional Democrats moved closer to a deal yesterday that would allow the federal government to insure hundreds of thousands of mortgages, even for delinquent borrowers, in an effort to revive the housing market. (published 0142 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ====== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ====== \par  \par =FOCUS: S&P SEES END IN SIGHT FOR BANK WRITE-DOWNS    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  is painting a rosier outlook for the troubled banking sector, as the rating agency said it expects the ongoing credit crisis to be near its end, although it warned of more heavy write-downs. (published 1716 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: S&P'S REASSURANCE IS A BIT RICH, REALLY    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Markets in Asia are breathing a sigh of relief Friday, courtesy of  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2 , but take with a grain of salt its prediction that we may be through the worst of it. (published 0022 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : DOLLAR MAKES RECOVERY TRY AFTER BIG FALL VS YEN    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar crawled out of a big hole against the yen Thursday as a rebound in the U.S. stock market allowed the greenback to grab back some of its sharp earlier losses that sent it to a 13-year low against the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 2030 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par LONG-DATED TREASURYS DOWN ON MISERABLE AUCTION, RECOVERING STKS    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Long-dated Treasurys were whacked Thursday afternoon, giving up a steep rally as a miserable 10-year note sale and recovering stocks sapped safe-haven flows. (published 2005 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =RATE FUTURES REPORT:WEAK ECON VS INFLATION IN VOLATILE TRADE    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. interest rate futures markets sent mixed signals in volatile trading Thursday, as weak economic data prompted traders to price in stronger expectations for an aggressive cut in the key short-term interest rate next week. (published 2029 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: SLIPPING DOWN THE FISCAL SLOPE IN ASIA    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With the global credit market depressed and as the U.S. economy continuing to weaken, taking the rest of the world with it, we are going to see more countries succumb to the temptation to take their credit cards out for a spin. (published 2339 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VIEW: DOLLAR BELOW Y100 NOT SETTING OFF ALARM BELLS    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A change in a big round number sometimes leads policymakers to stand up and act on an issue, but the dollar's drop Thursday below the symbolic 100 level against the yen didn't seem to do the trick. (published 1748 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 14-03-08 0200GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080314e43e0001z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
