\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day   \b0\par\par\uc2 669 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 13:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MINS FRET OVER YEN, BUT NO HINT OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities expressed alarm about the dollar's fall close to the Y100-mark for the first time since 1995 but didn't offer any clues about whether or when they might take any countermeasures. (published 0124 ET)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECB TRICHET: DISORDERLY USD MOVES UNDESIRABLE FOR ECON GROWTH    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's president Jean-Claude Trichet is concerned with roiling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets which he sees as detrimental to global economic growth, according to an interview with French weekly Le Point on Thursday. (published 0626 ET)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECB BINI SMAGHI:\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SWINGS DAMAGING TO GROWTH - REPORT    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Excessive fluctuations in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates is detrimental to economic growth, European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  executive board member Lorenzo Bini Smaghi said in a newspaper interview published Thursday. (published 0339 ET)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: CARLYLE CAPITAL NEARS COLLAPSE; NO PACT IN SIGHT    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The credit crisis has claimed another victim. Carlyle Capital Corp. said late yesterday that it expects that its lenders will seize its assets, causing the likely liquidation of the fund. "Although it has been working diligently with its lenders, the company has not been able to reach a mutually beneficial agreement to stabilize its financing," the fund said in a statement. (published 0024 ET)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JPMORGAN CHASE CEO:SUBPRIME FINANCIAL MESS CLEANUP 50% DONE    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The financial clean-up of the subprime mortgage loan mess is about halfway complete, but U.S. home prices likely will continue to decline for at least another year,  \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Chase & Co.\f28 \uc2 \f2  Chairman and Chief Executive James Dimon said Wednesday. (published 0006 ET)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US TREASURY'S KIMMITT: US ECON IN PERIOD OF SLOWER GROWTH    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 US Treasury Deputy Secretary Robert Kimmitt Thursday said the U.S. is currently in a period of slower growth and that risks to the economy are slated to the downside, but stopped short of using the word recession. (published 0609 ET)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK INFLATION EXPECTATIONS HIT RECORD HIGH IN FEB    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rate at which U.K. consumers expect prices to rise over the coming 12 months hit a record high in February, making it unlikely that the Bank of England will cut its key interest rate next month. (published 0540 ET)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ====== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ====== \par  \par SPOT GOLD AT NEW RECORD HIGH ABOVE $993.05/OZ ON WEAK DLR    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spot gold prices hit a new record high Thursday as market participants said the period of consolidation has come to an end, helped by further U.S. dollar weakness and crude oil prices in new record territory. (published 0750 ET)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par *OIL FUTURES: NYMEX CRUDE AT NEW HIGH AS DOLLAR FALLS (published 0742 ET)  \par  \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES WILT ON CARLYLE FUND, DOLLAR WOES    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stock futures wilted Thursday after a fund managed by  \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Carlyle Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  admitted it's close to collapse, showing that a Federal Reserve-led boost of liquidity is having a limited impact on troubled credit markets and dragging the dollar below a key level for the first time since 1995. (published 0618 ET)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EUROPEAN STOCKS TUMBLE AS DOLLAR WILTS    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European stock prices plunged Thursday on renewed concerns about the weakness of the global economy and the fragility of the banking system. (published 0735 ET)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MIDDAY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : DOLLAR POUNDED; SELLERS IN CONTROL    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders have once again pounded the dollar in European trading hours, pushing it to a fresh record low against the euro and to significant lows against a range of other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0705 ET)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOCUS: FED'S FEELGOOD FACTOR FADES FAST    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Reserve's massive liquidity injection supporting credit markets has boosted global risk appetite and put carry trades back in play. (published 0426 ET)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =WSJA:DOLLAR DROP BELOW Y100 BOOSTS CHANCES OF JAPAN SLOWDOWN    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rapidly falling dollar marked a significant milestone in Japan for the first time in 12 years, threatening Japan's exporters and increasing the likelihood that the world's No. 2 economy would slow down significantly. (published 0748 ET) [ 13-03-08 1200GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080313e43d000n2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal276