\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar falls below 100 yen, hits record low vs euro   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Toni Vorobyova   \par \uc2 741 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 00:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Changes byline, adds quotes, updates prices)   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 13 (Reuters) - The dollar fell below the psychologically key 100 yen mark for the first time in over a decade on Thursday, as well as plumbing fresh record lows versus the euro, the Swiss francs and a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Investors remained on edge about the ailing U.S. economy and the likely extent of future interest rate cuts as the Federal Reserve battles to stave off a recession.   \par \par \uc2 News of troubles at hedge funds and subsequent slumps in equity markets came amid a growing sense that Fed plans to pump hundreds of billions of dollars of liquidity into the banking system will not be enough to prevent further writedowns, losses and possible bankruptcies.   \par \par \uc2 This risk averse environment benefitted the safe haven Swiss franc and low yielding yen.   \par \par \uc2 The break of the 100 mark in dollar/yen and the approach of key levels in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs made markets jittery -- one-week implied volatility in dollar/yen, a key pricing component in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options, surged to seven-month highs above 20 percent.   \par \par \uc2 "It's a broad fall of the dollar. The economic situation in the U.S. is really black, the market is now expecting more and more cuts from the Fed and we have more and more news of financials experiencing difficulties," said Carole Laulhere, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Societe Generale in Paris.   \par \par \uc2 "Even if the Fed tried to give liquidity to the market at the beginning of the week it was not enough to restore the confidence of market participants, and I think risk aversion will continue for the time being."   \par \par \uc2 The dollar dropped to 99.77 yen, according to Reuters data, a mark last seen in late 1995. By 1039 GMT it had recovered a little to 100.27 yen, but was still down 1.25 percent on the day and nearly 10 percent for the year to date.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar also hit a record low against a trade-weighted basket of six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 71.821 and a historic low at 1.0047 Swiss francs.   \par \par \uc2 With the Swissie approaching parity, investors were looking to see whether the  \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  welcomed the strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an inflation-fighting tool, or highlights its negative impact on growth.   \par \par \uc2 The SNB is due to issue a statement after its 1300 GMT rate decision, where policy is widely seen on hold at 2.75 percent.   \par \par \uc2 A rate decision is also due at the same time in Norway, where a small minority are expecting a hike to 5.5 percent.   \par \par \uc2 POLICYMAKERS: ALL TALK?   \par \par \uc2 In contrast to expectations of 75 basis points of Fed rate cuts this month, markets are only pricing in 50 basis points of ECB easing by the end of the year.   \par \par \uc2 The euro surged through $1.56 to reach $1.5624 according to Reuters data despite European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet expressing concern on excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.   \par \par \uc2 "These kind of remarks have not been threatening enough so far but the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk has to increase on a looming $1.60 euro/dollar level," CIBC World Markets said in a client note.   \par \par \uc2 There is also speculation about whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will resume \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a four-year break, although analysts noted that on the BOJ's trade-weighted basis the yen is still around 20 percent weaker than it was back then.   \par \par \uc2 "It is possible, though it will be harder to justify given the trade weighted yen is still so weak," said David Mann, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered in Hong Kong.   \par \par \uc2 Verbally, though Japanese officials -- including top financial diplomat Naoyuki Shinohara, prime minister Yasuo Fukuda and finance minister Fukushiro Nukaga -- said excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were undesirable. Nukaga, however, added that the latest moves reflected dollar weakness rather than yen strength.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar's slide came despite remarks from U.S. President George W. Bush on Wednesday that he would like to see a stronger dollar and expressed concern its falling value was one cause of soaring U.S. energy prices.   \par \par \uc2 Troubles at financial organisations have continued to materialise. Carlyle Capital Corp, is in default on about $16.6 billion of debt, while Drake Management is considering liquidating all three of its hedge funds. (Editing by Mike Peacock)   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 6)|LANGEN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|SXNA   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080312e43c0020h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
