\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Sakakibara:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Won't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  With Dlr Over Y90   \b0\par\par\uc2 537 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 03:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds more details on market reaction, interest rates, post of BOJ governor.)   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The dollar is likely to fall below the key level of Y100 in coming weeks, but the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets unless it falls below Y90, former Japanese Finance Ministry official Eisuke Sakakibara said Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 "I think the dollar-yen will head toward the 100 level and break 100 within a matter of the next two or three weeks," Sakakibara told CNBC Asia in an interview. An eventual break of Y100 is a "foregone conclusion" in the Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, he said.   \par \par \uc2 For the year, the yen and Chinese yuan will each rise some 10% to 20%, while the euro could fall to Y130-Y140, he said.   \par \par \uc2 Sakakibara, who led \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as vice minister for international affairs in the 1990s, added, "I would say that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not happen above Y90," because \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  can better tolerate a strong yen now than in the past and because "the U.S. government is against \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this level."   \par \par \uc2 Changes in the yen's real effective exchange rate mean that a dollar around Y100 now is equivalent in economic impact to a rate of Y125-Y130 some 10 years ago, Sakakibara said. He put the dollar's fair value at Y90-Y100.   \par \par \uc2 "In terms of the competitiveness of the Japanese industry, there's no problem," as "Japan could compete at Y85 or Y90," he said. "Of course, yen-denominated profit (from overseas \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) would be reduced because of appreciation of the yen, but it won't really affect the Japanese industry in any significant way."   \par \par \uc2 Markets reacted little to Sakakibara's remarks as his outlook is generally in line with market perceptions. The dollar, which touched an eight-year low of Y101.40 Tuesday, was at Y103.01 around 0225 GMT Wednesday; the euro was at Y153.61.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  faces more downward pressure as the Federal Reserve is likely to cut interest rates by 50 basis points Tuesday, narrowing U.S.-Japan interest-rate differentials and prompting the unwinding of yen-short "carry trades," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Sakakibara said Prime Minister Yasuo Fukuda faces a "very difficult decision" in getting a new head for the BOJ, but that political wrangling over the succession won't derail Japan's monetary policy.   \par \par \uc2 The opposition, which controls the Upper House of Parliament, Wednesday rejected Fukuda's choice of Deputy Gov. Toshiro Muto to head the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the incumbent's term expires March 19.   \par \par \uc2 Sakakibara said the odds are 50-50 that the premier will stick with Muto, who has been deputy governor for five years after having risen to the top of the Finance Ministry bureaucracy. He cited two other candidates whose names are "floating around" - former BOJ Deputy Gov. Yutaka Yamaguchi and Hiroshi Watanabe, a former vice finance minister for international affairs.   \par \par \uc2 In any event, though, "there won't be any confusion in monetary policy at the Bank of Japan," Sakakibara said.   \par \par \uc2 -By William Mallard and John Jannarone, Dow Jones CommentaryPlus; 65-6415-4031; billy.mallard@dowjones.com [ 12-03-08 0251GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080312e43c0002q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
