\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-Dollar edges up vs yen but rebound seen unlikely   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Rika Otsuka   \par \uc2 655 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 07:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 11 (Reuters) - The dollar edged up after sliding close to an eight-year low against the yen on Tuesday, as Tokyo share prices gained despite a fall on Wall Street.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to 101.42 yen in early trade, nearing an eight-year low of 101.40 yen struck on electronic trading platform EBS on Friday, but later trimmed its losses to stand at 101.75 yen, steady from late U.S. trading on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the dollar seemed unlikely to rebound sharply against the yen, given signs of further deterioration in credit markets with more rate cuts expected by the Federal Reserve.   \par \par \uc2 "There is an enormous amount of credit jitters in the market, weighing on the dollar," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a Japanese trust bank.   \par \par \uc2 Hurt by writedowns of U.S. subprime mortgages and related securities, banks are increasingly reluctant to extend credit to investors such as hedge funds, triggering a cycle of margin calls and forcing selling across markets such as those for high-quality U.S. mortgage bonds.   \par \par \uc2 Tokyo stock market's Nikkei average rose 1 percent, having rebounded from a 2-\u189\'00\'BD year low hit earlier on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 Equity market moves are considered a barometer of investors' risk appetite, and gains in share prices can bolster demand for carry trades, which involve selling low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the yen to buy higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and assets.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar kept some distance from an all-time low hit late last week. It rose against the euro on Monday after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet said it was concerned about "excessive exchange rate moves".   \par \par \uc2 The euro trimmed some of the previous day's losses, rising 0.1 percent to $1.5360 It hit a record high of $1.5465 on EBS late last week after a report showing the biggest U.S. job losses in five years reinforced expectations for further interest rate cuts by the Federal Reserve.   \par \par \uc2 Speculation that the Fed might lower interest rates from the current 3 percent before its scheduled meeting on March 18 has also spurred dollar selling.   \par \par \uc2 U.S. interest rate futures now fully price in a 75 basis point rate cut by the Fed this month and around a 10 percent implied chance for rates to be lowered by 100 basis points.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar slipped 0.1 percent against the Swiss franc to 1.0189 francs but stayed above an all-time low of around 1.0135 francs hit on Friday.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  UNEXPECTED   \par \par \uc2 The dollar's slide to an eight-year low against the yen has fuelled speculation about chances of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities.   \par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities have a history of restraining the yen's strength to maintain the competitiveness of exporters. The last time they sold yen to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise was on March 16, 2004, when the dollar was at about 108.60 yen.   \par \par \uc2 But this time, many market participants do not expect \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market even if the dollar falls below the psychologically important 100 level for the first time in more than 12 years.   \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be effective unless it was a coordinated action," said Hideki Hayashi, chief economist at Shinko Securities.   \par \par \uc2 Coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen unlikely at a time when other members of the Group of Seven have been calling on China to allow greater exchange rate flexibility, analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 "The hurdle for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains high," Hayashi said. "Meanwhile, the market is acting as if it knows that the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very low."   \par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Fukushiro Nukaga stuck to the ministry's usual line on Tuesday that the government was watching \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements carefully and said he had no comment on specific levels. (Additional reporting by Masayuki Kitano, Editing by Michael Watson)   \par \par \uc2 LANGEN|GNN|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080311e43b000d2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
