\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  business lobby not seeking yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 09:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 10 (Reuters) - The head of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's most powerful business lobby said on Monday the group would not seek government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem the yen's rise against the dollar as long as it stays around present levels.   \par \par \uc2  Fujio Mitarai, chairman of the Japan Business Federation (Keidanren), told a news conference exporters should be able to cope with dollar/yen exchange rates around 105 yen.   \par \par \uc2  "I don't think we will call for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a while, as long as exchange rates stay around precent levels," Mitarai said.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar was around 102.00 yen <JPY=> on Monday, down 0.7 percent on the day after hitting an eight-year low of 101.40 yen late last week.   \par \par \uc2  The last time Japanese authorities sold yen to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise was on March 16, 2004, when the dollar was trading at about 108.60 yen.   \par \par \uc2  Japan sold 35 trillion yen ($342 billion) in the 15 months to March 2004 to weaken the yen due to concerns that its excessive strength could weaken overseas demand for Japanese exports and hurt the nation's economic recovery.   \par \par \uc2  Mitarai also said the government had picked best candidates for the next governor and deputy governors of the Bank of Japan.   \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the government nominated deputy governor Toshiro Muto as the next \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief. It put forward Masaaki Shirakawa, a former BOJ executive director, and academic Takatoshi Ito as deputy governors. [ID:nT202776]   ($1=102.30 Yen)   (Reporting by Kentaro Hamada, writing by Rika Otsuka, Editing by Michael Watson)      \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-YEN/|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|U|M|D|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080310e43a000jf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
