\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Forex \highlight\uc2  Officials Give No Hints Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 04:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds background, level of yen.)   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Nakamichi \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Despite the yen's surge last week to multiyear highs versus the dollar, Japan's finance minister and his top lieutenant Monday didn't go beyond repeating that they're watchful of the exchange rate, suggesting yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't on the table yet.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar Friday revisited a low it reached in 2000 of Y101.40 as weaker-than-expected U.S. employment data stoked fears of a U.S. recession. A falling U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes Japanese exports more expensive on global markets, and coupled with slumping U.S. demand for products from Japan and elsewhere, it is fanning concern that the Japanese economy may also slow sharply.   \par \par \uc2 But Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities have yet to threaten steps to prop up the dollar, letting speculation grow that they'll stay quiet even if the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  breaks below the psychologically important level of Y100.00. Around 0245 GMT, the greenback was at Y102.31.   \par \par \uc2 "I can't comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, but I'd like to monitor their recent movements carefully," Finance Minister Fukushiro Nukaga told a group of reporters at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Naoyuki Shinohara, who is the ministry's most powerful \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bureaucrat, Monday also stuck to his boss's line.   \par \par \uc2 "We are carefully watching \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates," Shinohara told reporters.   \par \par \uc2 Some analysts believe the government's apparent tolerance for a rising yen are a result of its belief Japan's economy can withstand a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or because the U.S. opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't conducted yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since March 2004.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 10-03-08 0305GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080310e43a00067\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
