\par\par \b \uc2 Japan's ruling party debates sovereign wealth fund   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Yoko Nishikawa   \par \uc2 496 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2008\par 12:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 22 (Reuters) - A panel of ruling party lawmakers began debating on Friday whether Japan should launch a wealth fund to more actively manage public money, including pension funds and some of its $996 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.   \par \par \uc2 The new Liberal Democrat Party panel has been set up despite opposition from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  to moving any of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which it manages, into such a fund because of fears about potential losses.   \par \par \uc2 The idea of a sovereign wealth fund for Japan follows high profile investments by government funds in Singapore, China and the Middle East, which recently came to the aid of U.S. banks hit by the subprime crisis, including  \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  ,  \uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  and  \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  . [ID:nN15540608]   \par \par \uc2 A Japanese fund could have a substantial impact on financial markets if Tokyo cuts investments in very safe assets, such as U.S. Treasury bonds, in favour of more risky markets.   \par \par \uc2 "The country will not perform well if we don't study at all and instead be defensive and only think about potential losses," said Yuji Yamamoto, the head of the new panel.   \par \par \uc2 At its first meeting, the panel of LDP lawmakers met Japan's Pension Fund Association and discussed how the government might better invest pension funds for higher returns.   \par \par \uc2 But they also touched on whether part of Japan's massive foreign reserves, the world's second largest after China, could be more effectively managed through a wealth fund.   \par \par \uc2 Yamamoto told reporters after the meeting that caution was needed when managing foreign reserves as changes may affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and the relationship with the United States.   \par \par \uc2 But he added that it would be possible to gain the understanding of the United States if the debate only focused on profits made from foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Historical data on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has mostly taken the form of dollar buying, suggests most of Tokyo's hefty foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are held in U.S. assets, although the government refuses to reveal what it invests in.   \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Fukushiro Nukaga said on Friday that creating a wealth fund for Japan could involve high risk so a debate was needed on the purpose and management of such a fund.   \par \par \uc2 Rintaro Tamaki, the finance ministry's international bureau head, voiced opposition to a fund at a separate gathering of LDP lawmakers on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 In addition to worries about potential losses from taking higher risks, Tamaki said it was the job of the private-sector, not the government, to seek high returns in a democratic country such as Japan with advanced financial markets.   \par \par \uc2 He also expressed concern that aggressive investments by a government fund may distort financial markets and worsen Japan's relations with other countries. (Editing by Rodney Joyce)   \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/FUND|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|NAT|ABX|BNX|FUN|Z|GFN|SI|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080222e42m000vf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
