\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  VIEW:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Power To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  Limited As G7 President   \b0\par\par\uc2 977 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2008\par 19:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Riva Froymovich \par    A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--As Group of Seven president this year, Japan isn't going to pull any fancy moves in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Japan will hold the rotating seat of G7 president in 2008, responsible for hosting the upcoming annual summit and the meeting of leading industrialized nations finance ministers on Feb. 9 in addition to managing its agenda.   \par \par \uc2 But any changes to the meeting's public statement, a closely watched indicator of what government is in the hot seat for its monetary management, is far from likely - even though Japan is probably unhappy with the dollar's recent flirtation with the Y100 level amid market volatility stemming from U.S. economic turmoil.   \par \par \uc2 A higher yen value with key trade partners jeopardizes the sales of manufactured goods, Japan's bread and butter. The yen rose to a two-and-a-half-year high recently against the dollar. In New York Monday afternoon, the dollar was at Y106.74 from Y106.58 late Friday.   \par \par \uc2 But officials from the euro zone and U.S. favor a hands-off approach, and have pushed for the appreciation of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to relieve themselves of trade pressures with their faster-growing partners. U.S. policy makers argue that a relatively weaker dollar is part of balancing the global trade imbalance.   \par \par \uc2 "(The) most pressing question is whether the (\b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the rally," said James McCormick, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at  \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  in London.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen in March 2004, and other G7 members tolerated the move given the threat that deflation posed to the world's second largest economy. Since then, however, G7 tolerance of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  has diminished. Indeed, the group's argument that China - the star of recent G7 communiques - is manipulating its yuan would be weakened if one of its own were to do the same.   \par \par \uc2 "We are highly skeptical," said McCormick, given the emphasis that the G7 has put on markets determining \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.   \par \par \uc2 "(It) will be difficult for the Japanese to abandon this message - especially with Japan hosting," McCormick noted, adding that its in ability to act increases the likelihood of the dollar eventually reaching Y95.   \par \par \uc2 Thanos Papasavvas, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  management at Investosec Asset Management in London, agreed that "the fact that they're sitting at the head of the meeting puts even more pressure for (\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's presidency, then, will be more a responsibility than an opportunity to truly shift policy.   \par \par \uc2 The narrow chance of Japan even broaching the topic at the conference will come if there is a brisk slide of the dollar against the yen this week - an unlikely event. At that point, authorities would act between the Y102 and Y104 level against the dollar to prevent a free fall to Y100, said Papasavvas.   \par \par \uc2 In the last G7 communique, leaders repeated a now standard position: \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  values should reflect economic fundamentals and excess volatility is undesirable. It called on China to accelerated appreciation of its effective exchange rate, key to balancing the global trade deficit for the U.S.   \par \par \uc2 As president, Japan will continue to push this point, said Papasavvas - and that's about as aggressive as Japan's role of president will allow.   \par \par \uc2 "Further strengthening of other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be to Japan's advantage," he said. "Faster appreciation of the renminbi would help exports of Japan."   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  A Difficult Position \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Policy makers in Japan are arguably in the most difficult position to deal with downside risks to growth," noted Marc Chandler, global head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brown Brothers Harriman\f28 \uc2 \f2  in New York. "Despite experiencing the longest expansion in more than 50 years and historic increases in commodity prices, Japan has not been able to normalize monetary or fiscal policy. Therefore they seem particularly ill-prepared to deal with the economic downturn."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Business sentiment and consumer sentiment have deteriorated. The December Tankan survey stood at a two-year low and consumer confidence recently hit a four year low.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen's recent strength, then, is more a product of global conditions than Japan's internal situation, many analysts agree. Thus, it will take a U.S. turnaround for the yen to pare back its gains.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui recently said he wants to discuss the issues surrounding the current global financial market instability with his G7 counterparts.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The G7 discussed in its October meeting the problems that are causing the current global financial market turmoil. At the coming forum, as chairman of the meeting, I would like to further discuss the issues and want to issue a G7 message that will help regain financial market stability," he said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Fukushiro Nukaga has added that G7 officials will discuss the impact of rating agencies and oil prices.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The last time Japan held the G7 presidency, the yen was very strong and the leadership focused on reducing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility, said Robert Fullem, vice president of corporate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sales in New York at  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi UFJ Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  "I think they're going to end up doing the same thing this year."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Riva Froymovich, Dow Jones Newswires; 201 938 5063; riva.froymovich@dowjones.com    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Riva Froymovich covers \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets for Dow Jones Newswires in New York.)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Katie Martin in London contributed to this report.)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments [ 02-04-08 1343ET ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 1141   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020080204e4240005e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
