\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Japan Econ Policymakers Keeping Hands Off Markets   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi and Takeshi Takeuchi   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2008\par 03:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Despite plummeting Tokyo stocks and a resurgent yen, Japanese policymakers Tuesday voiced optimism toward the domestic economy and indicated they aren't mulling any new steps to calm jittery markets.   \par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, the yen strengthened to its highest level in two and a half years at Y105.61 per U.S. dollar, meaning that Japanese exports are getting less competitive abroad. The benchmark Nikkei 225 Stock Average index closed the morning session down 4.4% at 12738.31.   \par \par \uc2 Those moves came as more and more investors are becoming convinced that the U.S. economy - the world's biggest customer for Japanese exporters - is headed for a sharp slowdown.   \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Fukushiro Nukaga said at a regular news conference Tuesday that he will keep a close eye on market developments and economic indicators. But he said the government has no intention for now of starting to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as aggressively as it did several years earlier to stem rises in the yen.   \par \par \uc2 "We're not thinking about it and that's also something we should not comment on," Nukaga said.   \par \par \uc2 Nukaga made similar comments in an interview with Dow Jones Newswires on Monday, saying that "we are not thinking about" large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for now.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold an unprecedented Y35 trillion for dollars in the 15 months through March 2004, to prevent a strengthening local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from hurting exports and snuffing out a then-nascent recovery in the economy. But since then, it has stayed out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.   \par \par \uc2 Economy Minister Hiroko Ota, in a separate press conference, struck a similar chord.   \par \par \uc2 "Because the market volatility stems from the U.S. subprime loan issue and concerns over its economy, it is difficult to take any steps (against the Japanese markets)," she said. "While the risks (to Japan's economy) are growing, I don't see any need for pump-priming measures at present."   \par \par \uc2 Comments from the key Japanese economy ministers highlight how rocky financial markets and a string of indicators hinting at decelerating U.S. and Japanese economic growth haven't yet overwhelmed the government's optimism.   \par \par \uc2 Nukaga said the world's economy is on "a solid footing" and that he hopes the latest stimulus package announced Friday by U.S. President George W. Bush will support the American economy. "I expect the (domestic) economic recovery will continue" as well, he said.   \par \par \uc2 Ota, though optimistic, tried to walk a more careful line.   \par \par \uc2 "The economy has kept recovering as recent production data show, but downside risks are growing these days," she said.   \par \par \uc2 Ota also said she expects the Bank of Japan, now holding a policy meeting that ends later in the day, will make an appropriate decision after considering volatile market moves.   \par \par \uc2 "I believe the BOJ will make a decision with these market volatilities in mind."   \par \par \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to announce its decision sometime after 0300 GMT. Economists expect the bank will keep its policy rate unchanged at 0.5%.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Takashi Nakamichi and Takeshi Takeuchi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com; takeshi.takeuchi@dowjones.com \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 22-01-08 0242GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080122e41m0005g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
