\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Nukaga: Big-Scale  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Not On Our Mind   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi and Takeshi Takeuchi   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 768 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2008\par 13:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Japanese government has no intention for now of resuming the huge \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  it conducted in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market several years ago, though authorities are still watching the yen's moves, Japan's finance minister said Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Fukushiro Nukaga's remarks suggest that Tokyo is keeping open its option of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening too much, but it's not worried enough to restart selling the yen as aggressively as it once did.   \par \par \uc2 Japan sold an unprecedented Y35 trillion for dollars in the 15 months through March 2004, to prevent a strengthening local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from hurting exports and snuffing out a then-nascent recovery in the economy. But since then, it has stayed out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets even though the yen has sometimes risen sharply, reasoning that it's best for the market to determine \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.   \par \par \uc2 Nukaga indicated that Japan isn't ignoring the yen's recent appreciation on worries about the U.S. economic outlook and increased risk aversion. The dollar fell to a two-and-a-half-year low of Y105.67 late Monday. However, that doesn't mean Tokyo is ready to rush back into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2 "We will continue to watch \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves carefully," Nukaga told Dow Jones Newswires in an interview. But asked whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is poised to resume its aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign of several year ago, Nukaga said, "we are not thinking about it" for now.   \par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent surges, coupled with signs of a slowdown in the nation's economy, have made some traders speculate that Tokyo may try to undercut the yen through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which sets \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, appears reluctant to order market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - it fears that such action won't be accepted by Group of Seven rich country counterparts given that in spite of some sluggish signs, the Japanese economy is doing much better than in years past.   \par \par \uc2 G7 finance ministers are due to meet in Tokyo on Feb. 9.   \par \par \uc2 An official familiar with the MOF's thinking recently told Dow Jones that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is possible "only if the Japanese economy is in the middle of a big crisis like it was between 2003 and 2004," when the country seemed on the verge of falling into a deflationary spiral.   \par \par \uc2 Still, the dollar is now below the Y106.60-level that a government survey last year said was the break-even point for Japanese exporters. That suggests that if the yen remains strong, Japanese exporters' profitability could suffer.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Economy Expanding Mildly \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turning to the Japanese economy, Nukaga said it remains in a "mild expansionary trend," though the momentum of its growth has recently "softened" and some parts of the economy are weak.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In spite of the weakness in Japan's stock market due in part to global economic worries, Nukaga said the government has no intention of taking steps to shore up share prices, as it did in the early 1990s.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We aren't considering any (special) measures for stock prices," Nukaga said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo shares Monday hit a new two-year low, with the benchmark Nikkei 225 Stock Average losing nearly 4% to end at 13,325.94, as investors expressed doubts about whether the latest stimulus plan by U.S. President George W. Bush could prevent a recession. Investors speculate that a sharp U.S. slowdown will drag Japan's economy lower because Americans buy more Japanese products than any other nation's people.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nukaga said, however, that Japanese assets must be made more attractive for foreign investors by taking policy steps such as ones that would improve the country's financial system.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "In the medium to long terms, stock prices have toreflect our national economy's attractiveness," he said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We need to face up to the fact stock prices reflect how attractive (Japanese assets are) as investment."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Takashi Nakamichi and Takeshi Takeuchi, Dow Jones Newswires, 813-5255-2929; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Corrected Jan. 21, 2008 08:59 ET (13:59 GMT) [ 21-01-08 1225GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan sold an unprecedented Y35 trillion for dollars in the 15 months through March 2004, to prevent a strengthening local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from hurting exports and snuffing out a then-nascent recovery in the economy.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ("=INTERVIEW: Nukaga - No Intention To Resume Huge \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Action," published at 1225 GMT, incorrectly stated that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  period was from January 2003 through July 2004.) [ 21-01-08 1302GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080121e41l000qy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
