\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan foreign reserves hit record high for 4th mth   \b0\par\par\uc2 440 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2007\par 03:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, background)   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 7 (Reuters) - Japan's foreign reserves, the world's second largest, rose to a record $954.5 billion at the end of October, partly because lower U.S. interest rates boosted the value of U.S. bonds held in the reserves, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 The reserves edged up 0.9 percent from $945.6 billion at the end of September, rising for the fifth consecutive month and marking a record high for the fourth month in a row, a finance ministry official said.   \par \par \uc2 The yield on the benchmark 10-year U.S. Treasury note fell to 4.475 percent at the end of October from 4.590 percent at the end of September, the official said.   \par \par \uc2 The euro's rise against the dollar inflated the value of euro-denominated bonds in the reserves, he said.   \par \par \uc2 The euro traded at $1.4487 at the end of October, up from $1.4267 a month earlier.   \par \par \uc2 Japan's reserves are second only to those of China, which had about $1.434 trillion in external reserves as of the end of September.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves ballooned after yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that amounted to a record 20 trillion yen ($175 billion) in 2003 and a further 15 trillion yen in the first three months of 2004, as Tokyo tried to keep a rapid rise in the yen from derailing a fragile economic recovery and accelerating deflation.   \par \par \uc2 Tokyo has kept out of the market since then, but the reserves have continued to grow steadily, partly on interest rate income from deposits and bonds held in the reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Income gains from Japan's reserves amounted to 3.692 trillion yen in fiscal 2006/07 ended in March this year, with interest on investment assets averaging 4.0 percent, the finance ministry said.   \par \par \uc2 The reserves in October included $804.839 billion in securities and $125.420 billion in deposits. The rest includes IMF reserve positions, special drawing rights and gold stocks.   \par \par \uc2 The government does not disclose the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  breakdown of the external reserves. But historical data on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has mostly taken the form of dollar buying, suggests most of Tokyo's hefty reserves are in dollars.   \par \par \uc2 Japan has been reluctant to diversify its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and seek higher returns by making active investments, unlike many other countries that have recently been investing part of their reserves in stocks and other high-risk, high-return assets. (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Mike Miller)   \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071107e3b70007s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
