\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: U.S. Automakers Complain That Yen Is 'misaligned'   \b0\par\par\uc2 813 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2007\par 00:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 By Lisa Twaronite   \par \par \uc2 SAN FRANCISCO (Dow Jones) -- Economists for Detroit's Big Three automakers fired another round Tuesday in their long battle against what they believe is Japan's undervalued yen, but \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts said the chances of any policy response were remote.   \par \par \uc2 Japan's "misaligned \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 " has created "huge distortions and dangers to global financial markets," in addition to a competitive disadvantage to U.S. automakers, said the Automotive Trade Policy Council (ATPC), an industry group whose members include  \uc2 Chrysler LLC\uc2 ,  \uc2 Ford Motor Company\uc2  (F) and  \uc2 General Motors Corp.\uc2  (GM) .   \par \par \uc2 The chief economists for the three companies called on Japan's new government to dramatically change direction and allow the yen to strengthen.   \par \par \uc2 In addition to outright \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as official "jawboning" the yen lower through official comments directed at markets, Japan "has pursued an ultra low interest rate policy, which has fueled the dangerous carry trade, and maintained pressure keeping the yen low," said General Motors Chief Economist Mustafa Mohatarem.   \par \par \uc2 Carry trades involve borrowing money in countries which have low interest rates and investing it in higher-yielding assets. As Japan's benchmark interest rate, at 0.5%, is the lowest in the developed world, the yen is a popular \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for such trades.   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan has kept interest rates near zero and flooded the financial system with funds, to help pull the country out of more than a dozen years of stop-and-go recession and a dangerous deflationary spiral.   \par \par \uc2 While \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since March 2004, its low interest rates have helped keep the yen from appreciating.   \par \par \uc2 "The Japanese yen is reflecting the underlying fundamentals of interest rate expectations," said Gareth Sylvester, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HiFX.   \par \par \uc2 In addition to non-Japanese investors borrowing the yen for carry trades, yield-hungry Japanese domestic investors continue to turn to investments outside their country for higher returns.   \par \par \uc2 "Not just funds, but even Japanese housewives are investing overseas, looking for the yields, and that's complimenting the carry trade," Sylvester said. "The level of the yen reflects this."   \par \par \uc2 Competitive disadvantage   \par \par \uc2 There's no question that a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  helps exporters by making their goods more attractively priced in overseas markets and boosting the value of their repatriated profits.   \par \par \uc2 "The artificially weak yen provides a significant advantage to Japanese automakers to the tune of $4000 to $12,000 per automobile and is the one competitiveness issue that is outside the control of our companies," said Ford chief economist Ellen Hughes-Cromwick.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. auto makers are not alone in describing the yen as undervalued.   \par \par \uc2 In its latest report on the global economy, the International Monetary Fund said there was room for the yen to appreciate, even as it trimmed its growth projection for Japan's economy next year to 1.7% from its previous forecast of 2.0%.   \par \par \uc2 Last week, Jean-Claude Juncker of Luxembourg, who heads a group of finance ministers from the nations that participate in the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , singled out the yen and China's yuan when the group gathered in Washington for the Group of Seven industrialized nations meeting.   \par \par \uc2 Japanese finance ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials asserted at the meeting that Japan's economic recovery is well under way, and Juncker said this should be reflected in exchange rates.   \par \par \uc2 "We have a house view that the yen is misaligned -- though 'undervalued' is probably a better word -- using longer-term models," said Dustin Reid, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro. "We think the yen should be trading in the 100-to-110 area against the dollar, perhaps 10% above where it is now," he said.   \par \par \uc2 "But I don't think at the end of the day they can do a whole lot, except backdoor diplomacy," he said, when asked about the chances of compelling Japan to take steps to boost its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Japan's "\b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to do what it's going to do," he said.   \par \par \uc2 In fact, since the undervalued yen has taken a back seat to the even more undervalued yuan these days, auto makers can't even count on U.S. officials to pay lip service to their cause.   \par \par \uc2 The auto economist's press conference came nearly a year after the leaders of the Big Three visited the White House, where they met with President Bush and Treasury Secretary Henry Paulson and called on them to push Japan to boost the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 At that time, the dollar was trading in a range of 115 yen to 120 yen. The dollar is now trading around the low end of that range.   \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Paulson had harsh words for the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies of an Asian country -- but it wasn't Japan. Instead, Paulson called on China to let its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen. [ 10-23-07 1825ET ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020071023e3an000dz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
