\par\par \b \uc2 ECB's Draghi:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  To Weaken Euro May Not Work   \b0\par\par\uc2 213 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2007\par 11:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Corrected Oct. 10, 2007 5:27 ET (9:27 GMT) [ 10-10-07 0923GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 ROME (Dow Jones)--European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Mario Draghi said Wednesday that achieving a weaker euro wasn't easy, adding that joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to soften the euro may not work.   \par \par \uc2 Answering a question from a senator at a parliamentary hearing in Rome about the benefits of a euro at $1.2, he replied "you have to take it there and it's not easy. Joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be needed."   \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.41 earlier Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Draghi, who is the governor of the Bank of Italy, added that a previous attempt by central banks to influence the value of the euro didn't have lasting effects.   \par \par \uc2 The ECB, the U.S. Federal Reserve and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2000 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to prop up the value of the euro after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit an all-time low against the dollar of below EUR0.85.   \par \par \uc2 It was the last time the world's biggest central banks acted in concert.   \par \par \uc2 -By Luca Di Leo and Liam Moloney, Dow Jones Newswires; +39 06 678 2543; liam.moloney@dowjones.com [ 10-10-07 1002GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020071010e3aa000hx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
