\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Europe should focus on yuan, not dollar at G7   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven C. Johnson   \par \uc2 837 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2007\par 22:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 2 (Reuters) - European officials alarmed by the sharp slide in the dollar may be better off focusing on the weak Chinese yuan if they want to rebalance global growth and ease pressure on the euro exchange rate.   \par \par \uc2 The euro surged to a record high just shy of $1.43 this week, increasing European anxiety that the dearer euro will stunt euro-zone growth by making exports more costly.   \par \par \uc2 And with Group of Seven finance ministers and central bankers set to meet Oct. 19-21, officials from Paris to Brussels to Frankfurt have stepped up their rhetoric and attempted to rope Washington into efforts to stem the dollar's slide.   \par \par \uc2 Fat chance, say \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists and economists.   \par \par \uc2 That's because they say the U.S. Treasury won't back efforts to prop up the dollar until Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , notably China's yuan, are allowed to strengthen and float more freely.   \par \par \uc2 "The issue isn't that the dollar should adjust but that the Asians should do their share," said Adam Posen, senior fellow at the Peterson Institute for International Economics in Washington.   \par \par \uc2 "The Americans will say to Europeans who are complaining: 'We warned you that if you didn't stand with us against the Chinese, you'd get stuck bearing the burden (of the dollar decline),'" he added.   \par \par \uc2 Washington has long insisted that an undervalued yuan gives China an unfair trade advantage and has urged Beijing to allow it to rise more rapidly against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 G7 officials have said as much at previous meetings, too. In April 2006, they urged emerging economies with large trade surpluses such as China's to free up their exchange rates and let \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  values reflect economic fundamentals.   \par \par \uc2 This was deemed essential to chipping away at destabilizing imbalances between countries like China that save too much and the United States, which saves too little.   \par \par \uc2 "Frankly, I think Treasury is quite happy with the dollar where it is," said Mike Moran, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Standard Chartered in New York.   \par \par \uc2 Added Paresh Upadhyaya, who manages some $29 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets at  \uc2 Putnam Investments\uc2  in Boston: "If it was a more disorderly decline in the dollar, then it would be more of an issue. But because it has been so gradual, I don't expect it to be on the formal agenda."   \par \par \uc2 UNEQUAL BURDENS   \par \par \uc2 The dollar has been steadily falling against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent years, and in the last two years or so the U.S. trade shortfall has stabilized around $60 billion.   \par \par \uc2 The latest decline in the greenback was triggered by the Federal Reserve's half-percentage point reduction in its benchmark interest rate last month. Meanwhile, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not signaled a similar move in the offing. At least, not yet.   \par \par \uc2 The euro's record high hit this week at $1.4281 is some 17 percent above where it stood in January 2006. Sterling has surged 16 percent in that time from around $1.74 to $2.04, while the Canadian dollar hit parity with the greenback in September for the first time since 1976.   \par \par \uc2 But China's yuan has climbed only about 6.5 percent since January 2006, and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in the world's fourth largest economy have exceeded $1 trillion.   \par \par \uc2 In a note to clients this week,  \uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  strategists brought the global imbalances that affect exchange rates into sharper focus when they noted that just 13 percent of the U.S. trade deficit is measured in G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the euro or sterling. The rest is with emerging market countries, many of which, like China, do not let their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  float freely.   \par \par \uc2 "The euro, you could argue, is getting up where it maybe shouldn't be, but the issue comes back to getting China to let their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  move more freely," said Posen.   \par \par \uc2 What's more, the Europeans may have a hard time getting other G7 countries on board. On Tuesday, a UK government source told Reuters that exchange rate policy would not be up for discussion at the G7 gathering.   \par \par \uc2 And Europe is hardly likely to find a willing partner in the Japanese. Though \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2004, the yen has remained the laggard among major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , up only 2 percent against the dollar since early 2006.   \par \par \uc2 "From Japan's perspective, the dollar isn't declining and they can honestly say that the market is setting the rate, which makes them natural allies with the United States," said David Gilmore, partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics in Essex, Connecticut.   \par \par \uc2 That may leave Europe -- rebuffed by the Americans and vexed by the Chinese -- to act on its own to try to cool the euro's gains, possibly by keeping interest rates on hold.   \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Kevin Plumberg)   \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /G7 (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|G|RBN|J|UKI|CANT|Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071002e3a2001l9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
