\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Japan MOF's Shinohara: watching  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  carefully   \b0\par\par\uc2 437 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2007\par 03:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds background)   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 17 (Reuters) - Japan's new top financial diplomat, in his first public comment since taking up the job last month, stuck to the finance ministry's standard line on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday as the yen surged towards a 14-month peak against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "As always we are watching \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markers carefully. We will not comment on specific levels," Naoyuki Shinohara, vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters as he arrived at work in the morning.   \par \par \uc2 The yen leapt in volatile trade on Thursday as investors unwound risky trades financed by using the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy high-yielding assets, on fears of a global markets shake-out.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar was near 113.40 yen <JPY=> at 0200 GMT on Friday, after having slid to a low of around 112 yen on Thursday, the lowest since June 2006.   \par \par \uc2 The yen's rapid movement prompting some traders to speculate that Japanese authorities could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, but any imminent move was still seen unlikely.   \par \par \uc2 "I think there is zero possibility for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Toru Umemoto, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at  \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  in Tokyo. "Policymakers still need to see how this will affect the economy.   \par \par \uc2 "Plus, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and that has been praised by the United States, while global leaders have called on China to stay out of the market ... If they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  now, it will only cause abnormal moves," Umemoto added.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a history of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent the yen's rise from hurting the country's economy. During its last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign, it sold 35 trillion yen ($306 billion) in a 15-month period to March 2004.   \par \par \uc2 But it has stayed out of the market since, even when the dollar fell as low as 101 yen in 2005, the longest Tokyo has gone without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on current records dating back to 1991.   \par \par \uc2 Officials at \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF), which is in charge of the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, usually change their terminology on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when they want to send signals to the markets.   \par \par \uc2 When \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market several years ago, MOF officials used to step up their rhetoric, often saying that they would "take appropriate action on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as needed".   \par \par \uc2 Shinohara replaced Hiroshi Watanabe in July and now takes charge of the ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, working directly with Finance Minister Koji Omi. ($1=114.50 Yen)   \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/SHINOHARA (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|NAT|ABX|BNX|FUN|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070817e38h0000m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
