\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-ECB's Bini Smaghi defends  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  division of labour   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gavin Jones   \par \uc2 647 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2007\par 10:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds ECB's Trichet, Bundesbank's Weber on EU treaty)   \par \par \uc2 ROME, July 3 (Reuters) - A top European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official on Tuesday defended the way the bank and ministers share responsibility for the euro, rebuffing calls for finance ministers to have more influence over \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.   \par \par \uc2 ECB Executive Board member Lorenzo Bini Smaghi also called for finance ministers to coordinate their message on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  matters better, saying they should present a united front.   \par \par \uc2 The division of labour between the ECB and euro-zone finance ministers worked more efficiently than the system in the United States and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , where finance ministries are responsible for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said in a speech to corporate and government officials in Rome.   \par \par \uc2 Effective \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed backing from domestic policy, especially interest rates; to be coordinated with other central banks; and to be well explained to markets.   \par \par \uc2 "The three above-mentioned conditions are best met if both the finance ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are involved in the definition of the policy," Bini Smaghi said.   \par \par \uc2 France is pressing for the euro to be used as an instrument to promote economic growth. Last month it abandoned plans to alter the ECB's mandate as part of a new European Union treaty. But Paris is still pushing for what it terms improved economic governance in the euro zone and more input from finance ministers on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.   \par \par \uc2 In separate comments, ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet and Governing Council member Axel Weber welcomed EU leaders' agreement on the outlines of the new treaty, which left the ECB's mandate unchanged.   \par \par \uc2 "I am very happy that the German presidency could work out a consensus amongst the European council," Trichet said at the International Centre for Corporate Culture and History in Frankfurt.   \par \par \uc2 Bini Smaghi said the shared responsibility for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy was not expected to change in talks on the details of the treaty, which current EU president Portugal hopes to finalise by mid-October.   \par \par \uc2 Under the current system, finance ministers define the exchange rate regime in consultation with the ECB and European Commission, and they can lay out a general orientation for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, although they have never set guidelines on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. The ECB is responsible for \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 MORE DISCIPLINE NEEDED   \par \par \uc2 In his speech, Bini Smaghi repeated his call for a single European voice to represent the euro on international bodies such as the Group of Seven meetings of finance ministers and central bankers.   \par \par \uc2 He called it a "pretext" to say more EU political integration was needed before that could happen and cited the agreement to have one EU foreign minister. "Could this decision also represent a way forward in the field of the external representation of the euro area?" Bini Smaghi asked.   \par \par \uc2 Better coordination among finance ministers on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  matters is needed, he said, noting contradictory public statements, for example in the lead-up to the Essen Group of Seven meeting in February, which tended to weaken the euro zone's position.   \par \par \uc2 Some policymakers expressed concern about the strength of the euro, especially against the yen, and some said it was appropriate. "These differences of opinion did not ultimately contribute to a strengthening of the yen," he said.   \par \par \uc2 "It is my opinion that the euro area is fully equipped to manage its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but better discipline is required in the preparation of the euro area's position to ensure a consistent message is sent to its partners."   \par \par \uc2 Bini Smaghi did not touch on euro-zone interest rates, ahead of a rate-setting meeting on Thursday when the ECB is expected to leave its benchmark cost of credit on hold at 4 percent. (Additional reporting by David Milliken in Frankfurt)   \par \par \uc2 ECB/BINISMAGHI (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|BNX|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070703e373000i8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
