\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Market wary but not intimidated by NZ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kazunori Takada   \par \uc2 861 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2007\par 06:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON, June 22 (Reuters) - Raids by New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets have failed to stop the high-flying kiwi dollar from hitting fresh 22-year highs and left it with a dilemma - when to strike again for maximum impact at minimal cost.   \par \par \uc2  On each of the past two Mondays -- when offshore markets were closed and trading volumes thin -- the Reserve Bank of New Zealand stepped in to cap the rise in the kiwi dollar, which has rallied to its highest levels since it was floated in 1985.   \par \par \uc2  "You'd have to be a little bit more wary on a Monday for the next few weeks because that is the time when \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is most likely to have impact," said Anthony Byett, managing director at a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  advisory firm fxmatters.co.nz.   \par \par \uc2  But keeping to such timing would be predictable, undermining the effectiveness of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  "As we've seen this Monday, interbank dealers will be more prepared now," he said.   \par \par \uc2  The New Zealand dollar plunged nearly 2 percent after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on June 11, the first time it had done so since the New Zealand dollar was released from a fixed-rate policy to trade freely on international markets.   \par \par \uc2  But the second \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had a limited and short-lived impact.   \par \par \uc2  The RBNZ, which has said it was concerned the high exchange rate could damage the export sector, confirmed its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but not the second.   \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rate of 8 percent -- the highest in the industrial world -- has made the New Zealand dollar a major investment target.   \par \par \uc2  Many investors fund their purchases of New Zealand assets by borrowing in a low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the yen. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in Japan are just 0.5 percent.   \par \par \uc2  The kiwi rose as far as $0.7660 <NZD=> <NZD=D2> on Thursday, a fresh post-float peak and an all-time high on a trade-weighted basis <=NZD>.   \par \par \uc2  TREND NOT A FRIEND   \par \par \uc2  While the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has made some investors more cautious about buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some analysts think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot fight the trend of global demand for higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  "I think they misread what the psychology was even before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Westpac Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Michael Gordon.   \par \par \uc2  Investors have remained wary but not put off by reports several times last week that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was inquiring about prices in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2  Masaaki Saito, assistant vice president of Gaitame.com, Japan's biggest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  margin-trading broker, said retail investors believe New Zealand's attractive yield difference outweighs the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest rate is only 0.5 percent while New Zealand is at 8 percent. In the end, it's that yield difference that individual investors are attracted to," he said.   \par \par \uc2  Reflecting global demand for yield, the New Zealand dollar is not the only high-flying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  In recent months, the British pound <GBP=> has scaled a 26-year high, the Canadian dollar <CAD=> a 30-year peak, and the Australian dollar an 18-year high <AUD=>.   \par \par \uc2  Both RBNZ Governor Alan Bollard and Bank of Canada Governor David Dodge have said the strength in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  can not be explained by domestic economic fundamentals.   \par \par \uc2  So far, the Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA) has been far more relaxed about its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in part because its strength helps keep down import prices and so restrains inflationary pressures.   \par \par \uc2  The RBA has also been more subtle in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , quietly selling the Australian dollars it bought between 1997 and 2001 when it was openly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  The selling has been routine since 2002 but was stepped up in the first four months of the year to reach over A$1 billion. Dealers suspect more has been offloaded since then.   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tends to play down this selling as an effort to rebuild reserves, but really it is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by any other name, analysts say. By keeping it quiet, the RBA avoids becoming a target for speculators while retaining the ability to inject some two-way risk into the market.   \par \par \uc2  Byett said the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may also step up its presence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2  "At some stage soon, I think you'll see the RBA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a more explicit manner than they've done to date this year," he said.   \par \par \uc2  Byett said the RBNZ would be more effective if it adopted an RBA style of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  The RBNZ can spend as much as it wants in kiwi-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it can only book \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses up to NZ$1 billion under an agreement with the government.   \par \par \uc2  Given the constraint, analysts estimate the RBNZ could spend around NZ$10 billion on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- just a fraction of the 35 trillion yen ($283 billion) the Japanese authorities sold in 2003 and 2004 to try to prevent a rapid rise in the yen from damaging a fragile economy.  (Additional reporting by Wayne Cole in SYDNEY)     \par \par \uc2 NEWZEALAND-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ND|AUF|J|UKI|NAT   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070625e36m0006m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
