\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Japan's Omi tweaks  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  speak,watches yen 'carefully'   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Yoko Nishikawa   \par \uc2 573 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2007\par 08:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments from analysts)   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, June 19 (Reuters) - Japanese Finance Minister Koji Omi appears to have tweaked his list of regular comments on the yen -- saying he now "watches \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates carefully."   \par \par \uc2 It's hardly verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but with the yen hitting record lows versus the euro and 4-1/2-year troughs against the dollar, any change in official Tokyo comments could be significant.   \par \par \uc2 In what may be an intentional signal, Omi, the minister in charge of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, started using the new phrase last Friday and repeated it on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 Omi reiterated that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should reflect economic fundamentals and that he would not comment on specific \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels -- two of his tried and trusted phrases.   \par \par \uc2 Then he added: "I would like to watch \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates carefully from now on," and noted that Japanese economic fundamentals are currently favourable.   \par \par \uc2 Asked if that meant the yen should strengthen rather than weaken, he again said: "I won't comment on specific \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, but I will continue watching their moves carefully."   \par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities usually change their rhetoric on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when they want to send signals to the markets. They have used the phrase "watching \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves" before to indicate that they are growing somewhat wary of market moves.   \par \par \uc2 So far, traders have paid little attention to Omi's remarks, said Toru Umemoto, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 Barclays Capital.\par \par \uc2 "If Japanese authorities don't like sed to step up their rhetoric, often saying that they would "take appropriate action on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as needed".   \par \par \uc2 The yen has fallen across the board since Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui said on Friday that he needed more evidence of sustained economic expansion before raising rates further, dousing expectations of a rate hike in July.   \par \par \uc2 Most market players expect the BOJ to raise rates to 0.75 percent in August, but that still pales in comparison with 5.25 percent in the United States and 4.0 percent in the euro zone.   \par \par \uc2 Any rate hike by the BOJ is unlikely to dull the allure of carry trades -- borrowing yen to buy higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- especially as many investors see the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifting rates twice more this year to 4.5 percent.   \par \par \uc2 YEN WEAKNESS OR EURO STRENGTH?   \par \par \uc2 Earlier in the year, Omi's European counterparts had fretted over the yen's weakness against the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Their concerns were highlighted when Group of Seven finance ministers met in Essen, Germany, in February, warning investors against betting on the yen in one direction when Japan's economy continued to strengthen. Omi also echoed such views then.   \par \par \uc2 But at the next G7 meeting in April in Washington, Omi said movements between the dollar, the euro and the yen since February pointed to euro strength rather than yen weakness.   \par \par \uc2 The yen's drop may now become a market focus again.   \par \par \uc2 The euro hit a fresh record high of 166.10 yen on Tuesday and the dollar was hovering around 123.60 yen staying near its 4-1/2-year high of 123.76 yen hit this week.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets from late 1997 to mid-1998 when the country was in a financial crisis and foreign investors were dumpinreuters.com)) ($1=123.64 Yen)   \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070619e36j000ae\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/0